.TH "libnvmf_read_hostid" 9 "libnvmf_read_hostid" "September 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_read_hostid \- Get the configured host identifier
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "char *" libnvmf_read_hostid
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
struct libnvme_global_ctx object
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Return \fIctx\fP's hostid default if one is set, otherwise read the
identifier from $SYSCONFDIR/nvme/hostid. $SYSCONFDIR is usually /etc.
An empty \fIctx\fP default suppresses the file lookup.

This is not the identity a connect uses. See \fBlibnvmf_host_get_ids\fP
for the full resolution order.
.SH "RETURN"
The host identifier, or NULL if unsuccessful. If found, the caller
is responsible to free the string.
